# Paths that must not merge on surveyor's approval alone.
#
# How this protects itself:
#   - GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the PR's base branch, so a PR that edits
#     this file is judged by the version already on main.
#   - GitHub Apps cannot be code owners, so a bot approval (surveyor's or any
#     other App's) can never satisfy an entry here.
#   - These entries only take effect once the main-branch ruleset turns on
#     "Require review from Code Owners" (see docs/DESIGN.md, "Merge policy").
#
# There is deliberately no catch-all `*` entry: anything not listed merges on
# surveyor's approval alone.

# This file and the automation around it.
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @mastersingh24
/.github/workflows/             @mastersingh24
/.github/dependabot.yml         @mastersingh24

# surveyor's own review config (surveyor dogfoods itself).
/.github/surveyor.yaml          @mastersingh24

# The code that decides approve vs. request-changes, and the code that
# resolves config (locked org keys, base-branch reads, opt-out handling).
/internal/verdict/              @mastersingh24
/internal/config/               @mastersingh24

# Instructions the reviewer always applies, including the prompt-injection
# rules. Changes here change what "approved" means.
/rubrics/core/                  @mastersingh24

# Deployment, IAM / Workload Identity, and the GitHub App permission manifest.
/deploy/                        @mastersingh24
/app-manifest.yaml              @mastersingh24

# CI gates for this repo.
/dev/ci/                        @mastersingh24
/dev/tools/.golangci.yml        @mastersingh24
